    "A works if “non-tax receipt” means non-tax revenue; E3.2 also makes receipts that reduce financial assets capital, and the stem omits that status.",
    "An asset-sale reading could make the second receipt capital, but the stem does not establish that reading as fact.",
    "E1.1 classifies tax revenues as revenue receipts, contradicting C’s classification of the tax receipt as capital.",
    "D reverses E1.1: receipts that do not lead to a claim on government are revenue receipts."
