      "premise_source": "excerpt",
      "evidence_id": "E1.1",
      "premise_quote": "Revenue receipts are those receipts that do not lead to a claim on the government. They are therefore termed non-redeemable. They are divided into tax and non-tax revenues.",
      "reason": "E1.1 places tax revenues within revenue receipts, so C’s capital classification of the tax receipt is false."
    },
